blames; it is also one company's water.\"}"},{"node":"nf4d76b02a0b0","v":1,"at":"1866-08-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"citation\":\"CL2 (claim) in https://hypgraph.com/examples/linked/broad-street, version 1: Houses supplied by the Southwark and Vauxhall Company had 315 cholera deaths per 10,000 houses against 37 for Lambeth — 8.5 times the rate, in the same streets.\",\"hash\":\"97f06a66e153807ed733ccb75138ab9d9fe0fccf87a397112001f42aacb36adc\",\"kind\":\"primary\",\"node\":\"ne00858e453b1\",\"record\":\"https://hypgraph.com/examples/linked/broad-street\",\"reliability\":\"Snow's comparison of the two south London companies: the result this inquiry repeats.\",\"retrieved\":\"1866-08-01T10:00:00Z\",\"says\":\"Houses supplied by the Southwark and Vauxhall Company had 315 cholera deaths per 10,000 houses against 37 for Lambeth — 8.5 times the rate, in the same streets.\",\"url\":\"https://hypgraph.com/examples/linked/broad-street/#node=ne00858e453b1\",\"version\":1}"},{"node":"ncf04deb18e9d","v":1,"at":"1866-08-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"predictions\":[\"Deaths concentrate in the company's district, whatever the district's elevation.\",\"Neighbouring districts on other companies' water are struck far less.\"],\"statement\":\"The epidemic followed the East London Water Company's supply: the water carried it, as it did in south London in 1854.\"}"},{"node":"n92bc6c5f65c0","v":1,"at":"1866-08-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"predictions\":[\"Low districts suffer alike, whichever company supplies them.\"],\"statement\":\"The east end suffered because it is low-lying and crowded: the elevation law.\"}"},{"node":"n75e47a94a115","v":1,"at":"1866-08-10T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"aim\":\"Map the epidemic's deaths onto the water companies' districts.\",\"controls\":\"Low-lying districts supplied by other companies.\",\"method\":\"deaths by water supply, district by district\",\"protocol\":\"Take the weekly death returns for each registration district and set beside them the company that supplies it; compare districts of similar elevation on different water.\",\"success_criteria\":\"The deaths follow one supply across elevations, or they follow elevation.\"}"},{"node":"naa48c3a046fd","v":1,"at":"1866-08-10T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"kind\":\"agent\",\"name\":\"Deaths by registration district and water company, 1866\",\"note\":\"Farr's own tabulation for the Registrar General, reported by him (an agent-reported run).\",\"state\":\"succeeded\"}"},{"node":"nd606bc9e014b","v":1,"at":"1866-09-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"kind\":\"observed\",\"outcome\":\"positive\",\"summary\":\"The deaths were concentrated in the districts supplied by the East London Water Company; low-lying districts on other companies' water were struck far less.\"}"},{"node":"n32f308a5c8b0","v":1,"at":"1866-09-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"kind\":\"observed\",\"outcome\":\"positive\",\"summary\":\"Part of the company's supply came from its reservoirs at Old Ford beside the River Lea, which the inquiry found had let in unfiltered water.\"}"},{"node":"n8ab83de875bf","v":1,"at":"1866-09-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"farr","reason":"","body":"{\"limitations\":\"Districts, not houses: a district's supply is mostly, not wholly, one company's.\",\"scope\":\"London, the 1866 epidemic, deaths by registration district and supplying company, set beside the 1854 comparison of the south London companies.\",\"statement\":\"The 1866 epidemic in east London followed the East London Water Company's supply, as the 1854 comparison of the south London companies did.\"}"},{"node":"ne49ab94cc778","v":1,"at":"1866-10-01T10:00:00+00:00","by":"radcliffe","reason":"","body":"{\"method\":\"My own inquiry into the east London outbreak for the Privy Council.\",\"notes\":\"The deaths follow the company's water; the Old Ford reservoirs are the